# CODEOWNERS — who must review what.
#
# This file only REQUESTS review on its own. It becomes a requirement when the
# v3base ruleset enables "Require review from Code Owners" (Settings -> Rules ->
# Rulesets). Until then, treat it as routing rather than as a gate.
#
# Both maintainers own everything, deliberately. The alternative — splitting
# ownership by area — creates paths that one person can land alone, and on a
# chain the areas that look safest to split (CI, dependency manifests) are the
# ones where a single unreviewed change does the most damage.
#
# Handles are the repository's two admin collaborators, verified against the
# API. An invalid or non-collaborator handle makes a rule silently fail to
# apply, so only add accounts with write access here.

# ── Everything ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*                                   @i-naman @saishibunb

# The entries below do not narrow the rule above; they restate it so that a
# future edit to the default line cannot quietly drop review on the paths where
# it matters most. GitHub applies the LAST matching rule, so each of these must
# name both owners too.

# ── CI and supply chain ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These decide what runs with repository secrets in scope, and what is allowed
# to reach a release. A change here can disable a gate without touching a line
# of Go — the change least likely to be noticed in review.
/.github/                           @i-naman @saishibunb
/.github/workflows/                 @i-naman @saishibunb
/.github/workflows/actions.lock     @i-naman @saishibunb
/.github/dependabot.yml             @i-naman @saishibunb
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @i-naman @saishibunb
/Dockerfile                         @i-naman @saishibunb
/.golangci.yml                      @i-naman @saishibunb
/.golangci-telemetry.yml            @i-naman @saishibunb

# ── Dependency manifests ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# go.mod/go.sum are the supply chain: a bump here changes what is linked into
# the node binary. govulncheck in CI reports; it does not decide.
/go.mod                             @i-naman @saishibunb
/go.sum                             @i-naman @saishibunb

# ── Consensus-critical ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A defect in these is a fleet-wide halt or a divergent ledger, not a bug on one
# node.
/Security/                          @i-naman @saishibunb
/consensus/                         @i-naman @saishibunb
/consensushash/                     @i-naman @saishibunb
/messaging/BlockProcessing/         @i-naman @saishibunb
/thebesync/                         @i-naman @saishibunb
/Sequencer/                         @i-naman @saishibunb
